## Should-fix 3: seed backfill guards (negative-path verified)

- nocobase-hub-modules.mts hub_as_assets: `row.tag ?? AST-####` — a
  hand-edited tag survives reruns.
- nocobase-crm-modules.mts crm_quotes: createdAt only backfilled when null.
- Negative path: hand-set tag=AST-HAND-EDIT (id 1) and createdAt=2026-05-05
  (id 1), reran both scripts → both values survived verbatim; crm_quotes
  backfill reported 0 rows for the guarded fields.

## Should-fix 4: project form binds the real column `no`

Root cause: the form field was `code` but hub_pj_projects ships `no` (no
`code` column) — AI fill showed the value in the UI while the API silently
dropped it (pre-existing id 20 row has NULL no). Fixed the whole read/write
chain, not just the AI binding: form.tsx (FormField/defaultValues ×2/aiFields)
+ types.ts (ProjectRecord/ProjectFormValues) + list.tsx (cell + CSV export) +
show.tsx + quick-search.tsx local type and secondary line.
Browser-verified: created「G9防重验证-中东清真认证二期」with 编号 PRJ-G9-001 →
hub_pj_projects id 21, no='PRJ-G9-001' non-null; the projects list now also
renders the seeded nos (PRJ-2026-022 etc. — impossible before, the reader
consulted a nonexistent column).

## Should-fix 5: create double-submit guard

submitting ref in the create handler (`if (submitting.current) return` +
finally reset). Browser-verified: three click() calls in one tick → exactly
1 row (17 → 18 rows, one G9-named row). The API-level idempotency key stays
registered for the H round (handoff 0.h G9 line).

